From 718849a7041b93e7cf49bceed1dca0079821d78b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:04:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] A browser sandbox, because jsdom cannot see the screen

Every test in scripts/ runs in jsdom, which has no layout engine: scrollTop is
always 0, every bounding box is zero, nothing has a height. So a whole class of
bug is invisible to the entire suite by construction -- the board jumping when
you click, a modal resizing under the pointer, a picker covering the text being
typed, a column flickering. Those are also the ones dispatchers notice first,
and the ones that make a deploy feel unsafe.

This runs the real pages in real Chromium against a fake Supabase:

- serve.mjs serves the repo exactly as Pages does, no build step, so what the
  browser runs is what ships.
- fake-supabase.js is served IN PLACE of supabase.min.js by route
  interception. addInitScript alone loses the race -- the real bundle loads
  after it, overwrites window.supabase, and the real GoTrue client redirects to
  login.html because there is no session.
- It also RECORDS realtime handlers, so a test can replay another dispatcher's
  edit landing mid-keystroke via window.__sandboxEmit(). That condition is
  behind several of the bugs already documented in CLAUDE.md and could not be
  staged any other way.

Two specs to start: the board holds its scroll position through click, type,
arrow and pick; the Text a Group modal opens checked, preselects nothing, and
does not change height when a rating is clicked.

One thing worth recording for whoever reads this next: the board scrolls inside
`.grid-scroll`, NOT the window. window.scrollY barely moves. Asserting on it
reports zero drift while the board slides several rows.

scroll-tracer.js is the companion for bugs that only appear on live data: paste
it into the console on the real board, use it until it jumps, then call
__whyDidItMove() for the stack that moved it. Observe-only.

