From 71c5fc8a4245e5bcede9fff438f076bb0bc509ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:13:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Sandbox: replay a redraw landing mid-edit, and trace the
 editor moving

From Ron's screen recording: he is typing a driver name into a BLANK row and
250ms later the editor is in the row ABOVE, with that row's existing name open
in an edit box and its own suggestion list. In the frames either side, the
blank row he was typing in has disappeared and everything below has shifted up
-- "it moves up 2 spaces".

That is the failure CLAUDE.md already describes, "the cursor jumping to the row
above after a redraw", in a shape the data-trip fix does not cover: a
placeholder row with no dbId, which is exactly the row a restore selector
cannot find again if it is rebuilt or pruned.

- focus-jump.spec.mjs stages it: type into a blank row under a filled one,
  land a realtime echo, and assert the cursor is still in the same row with
  the draft intact. It passes against synthetic blank rows, so the live board
  has a condition the fixtures do not -- most likely a true placeholder row
  being INSERTed mid-keystroke, where the realtime echo arrives before the
  local row has its dbId and handleRealtimeShiftChange adopts it as a second
  row. Left in place as the scaffold to finish against real evidence.

- fake-supabase: channel.send/track/untrack/presenceState were missing, so
  every realtime redraw threw "boardChannel.send is not a function" and the
  handler aborted before the part under test. Any realtime test written before
  this was passing for the wrong reason.

- scroll-tracer now records EDITOR MOVED (focus crossing to a different
  data-row) and ROWS CHANGED (rows added or removed from the tbody) alongside
  the scroll calls, because the recording shows the symptom is the editor
  moving and a row vanishing, not the container scrolling.

